WEBVTT

00:00:02.440 --> 00:00:06.650
<b>GUNDAM
VICTORY
MOBILE SUIT</b>

00:00:06.650 --> 00:00:12.610
The furious rain, Makes my heart shake
hageshii ame ga, kokoro wo yuruwaseru

00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:15.820
Like it did on that day
Ano hi no youni

00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:22.910
But I just ran through, In my dream I had till yesterday
Tada hashirinuketa, kinou made no MY DREAM

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:26.710
...I still believe
...shinjiteiru no sa

00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:34.470
I'm willing to fight, An endless defense
Owari no nai, defense demo ii yo

00:00:35.090 --> 00:00:42.350
As long as you, Keep on gazing at me
Kimi ga boku wo, mitsumetsuzukete kureru nara

00:00:42.730 --> 00:00:45.270
STAND UP TO THE VICTORY!

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:50.980
Turn to face all the mornings ahead, And someday
Ikutsumono asa wo mukae, Itsuka kitto

00:00:52.070 --> 00:00:53.860
Try to seize them
tsukande miseru

00:00:53.990 --> 00:00:56.450
STAND UP TO THE VICTORY!

00:00:56.780 --> 00:01:02.120
Even if nothing, Lies on the other side
Sono mukougawa ni, nanimonakutemo

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:06.040
It doesn't matter to me
kamawanai kara

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:14.050
...Just as long as I can embrace, Your gentle, irreplaceable smile!
Kakegae no nai, kimi no yasashii egao daite

00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:30.500
Having polluted the whole of Earth, mankind emigrated into space,

00:01:30.530 --> 00:01:33.660
ushering in an era in which it became a familiar home for him.

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:40.660
But, in space as on Earth, the human race repeated its history of war.

00:01:41.630 --> 00:01:48.330
Perhaps it was their instincts as they tried to adapt to a new environment...

00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:50.730
...that caused their foolishness to return.

00:01:53.100 --> 00:01:58.060
If people can't bring themselves to believe that they can live in space,

00:01:58.630 --> 00:02:01.930
mankind's history will be a tragic one.

00:02:05.860 --> 00:02:07.700
THE WHITE MOBILE SUIT

00:02:07.700 --> 00:02:09.460
"The White Mobile Suit".

00:02:09.460 --> 00:02:10.330
THE WHITE MOBILE SUIT

00:02:23.660 --> 00:02:25.760
How dare he use my test unit!

00:02:29.430 --> 00:02:31.060
Is this thing trashed?

00:02:36.500 --> 00:02:38.930
The next shot will be aimed at the cockpit, Pilot!

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:45.160
Dammit!

00:02:45.900 --> 00:02:46.760
There we go!

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:51.330
Emergency!

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:52.900
What?!

00:03:00.530 --> 00:03:04.400
The color of that jacket! It's the guy who jumped into my cockpit!

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:16.460
From that height... He couldn't have survived.

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:33.830
Uh-oh...

00:03:36.330 --> 00:03:38.000
Ow...

00:03:39.100 --> 00:03:40.760
My whole body aches...

00:03:42.160 --> 00:03:43.930
H-How?

00:03:48.930 --> 00:03:51.000
How did I end up in this situation?

00:03:51.660 --> 00:03:55.360
How was I able to pilot one of BESPA's mobile suits?

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:03.400
A little slower! It's not quite there, yet.

00:04:03.830 --> 00:04:06.760
We don't know when the fires from the bombings will be put out.

00:04:06.800 --> 00:04:10.160
I'll go look for Üso, so you stay here with the Camion.

00:04:10.200 --> 00:04:13.760
There's a box of diapers for Karlmann in the Camion's cabin.

00:04:13.800 --> 00:04:15.160
Oh, I see.

00:04:15.860 --> 00:04:20.130
I promise, I'll bring Üso back to Uwig. Don't worry.

00:04:20.260 --> 00:04:21.330
Thank you.

00:04:21.900 --> 00:04:23.260
There, there...

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:28.030
I'm saying this more for my peace of mind, but don't overdo it.

00:04:28.060 --> 00:04:29.900
Peace of mind can be its own diversion.

00:04:30.400 --> 00:04:31.300
Hi.

00:04:31.400 --> 00:04:32.430
I'm back!

00:04:37.460 --> 00:04:39.160
The wind's changed direction.

00:04:40.360 --> 00:04:41.460
I can move.

00:04:41.900 --> 00:04:44.900
Agh, my whole body hurts!

00:04:57.760 --> 00:05:01.560
Even though we weren't here yesterday, it happened all the same.

00:05:02.630 --> 00:05:04.900
Are you going home, Miss Katejina?

00:05:07.630 --> 00:05:12.230
I'm glad Uwig was bombed like this.

00:05:13.130 --> 00:05:18.130
Because the privileged who lived in the special quarter were all corrupt.

00:05:18.630 --> 00:05:21.930
Except no person should ever do something like this.

00:05:22.200 --> 00:05:24.430
That applies to all of human history, doesn't it?

00:05:24.460 --> 00:05:26.130
It's like Largaine, all over again.

00:05:26.560 --> 00:05:30.860
Odelo, don't let Shahkti and the others see this.

00:05:30.900 --> 00:05:34.260
I know. I won't let Suzy see it, either.

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:36.330
Count! Come here!

00:05:36.900 --> 00:05:41.630
This mass of corpses here. Aren't they from the factory?

00:05:42.800 --> 00:05:44.330
There are a lot of them.

00:05:47.030 --> 00:05:51.060
Isn't this Boysen? We'd arranged to meet him here!

00:05:51.760 --> 00:05:55.000
At least he has the map, Count.

00:05:55.230 --> 00:05:56.960
You're right.

00:05:57.400 --> 00:06:00.660
Boysen, that's the sort of man you were.

00:06:01.330 --> 00:06:05.960
But why would the foreman be here, away from the factory?

00:06:06.030 --> 00:06:09.160
Because he didn't want the enemy to know where it was.

00:06:17.460 --> 00:06:21.530
Miss Marbet's okay! Hey! Over here!

00:06:24.760 --> 00:06:25.800
That's weird.

00:06:26.530 --> 00:06:28.000
Hey!

00:06:31.700 --> 00:06:33.430
Where is that kid?

00:06:36.160 --> 00:06:38.600
Here she comes... Go!

00:06:46.330 --> 00:06:48.700
Üso! Are you there?

00:06:48.830 --> 00:06:53.330
Here! Over here, Miss Marbet! Miss Marbet!

00:06:55.300 --> 00:06:59.100
Miss Marbet! You're all right! Miss Marbet!

00:07:00.700 --> 00:07:01.960
Miss Marbet?

00:07:02.300 --> 00:07:03.900
Miss Marbet... Huh?

00:07:04.460 --> 00:07:06.930
Miss Marbet! Speak to me!

00:07:14.830 --> 00:07:16.960
You're saying that Sabat was shot down?!

00:07:17.000 --> 00:07:21.330
Yes, sir. I regret to inform you that he fought in vain.

00:07:21.630 --> 00:07:23.130
And you just left the Shokew?

00:07:23.160 --> 00:07:25.030
It's all right, Duprê.

00:07:25.400 --> 00:07:30.100
Ltjg. Cronicle Asher brought the Shokew safely back to base.

00:07:30.560 --> 00:07:33.430
You did your duty well.

00:07:33.730 --> 00:07:35.400
You can return to the homeland,

00:07:35.430 --> 00:07:37.630
now that you've gotten some combat experience.

00:07:37.660 --> 00:07:39.030
Is that so?

00:07:39.400 --> 00:07:42.230
The lieutenant has yet to achieve a true victory.

00:07:42.260 --> 00:07:47.100
Don't you actually want to mop up those League Militaire remnants?

00:07:47.360 --> 00:07:49.530
Lieutenant Duprê is correct.

00:07:49.700 --> 00:07:51.530
Then do as you wish.

00:07:51.600 --> 00:07:53.860
Yes, ma'am! I will.

00:08:02.100 --> 00:08:03.430
Turn left there.

00:08:03.460 --> 00:08:05.660
Where the old auto factory used to be?

00:08:07.160 --> 00:08:08.560
That building.

00:08:16.360 --> 00:08:19.100
Wait while we check underground.

00:08:19.130 --> 00:08:20.100
Sure thing.

00:08:21.330 --> 00:08:22.330
There, there...

00:08:22.360 --> 00:08:25.760
Hey, Odelo, there's no milk in the kitchen.

00:08:25.800 --> 00:08:28.500
Really? Oh, great...

00:08:28.800 --> 00:08:32.960
The old men said their friends were using the underground factory.

00:08:33.000 --> 00:08:35.460
They must have a big refrigerator down there.

00:08:39.700 --> 00:08:41.160
W-What's...?

00:08:48.860 --> 00:08:50.400
It's all thanks to Boysen.

00:08:50.900 --> 00:08:53.800
Thanks to the resistance they mounted in Uwig...

00:08:54.400 --> 00:08:59.600
As you can see, this factory was preserved.

00:08:59.900 --> 00:09:03.900
You're saying you sacrificed Uwig for your operation?!

00:09:03.930 --> 00:09:05.360
Just the opposite.

00:09:05.930 --> 00:09:09.530
Against an enemy bent on subjugating the entire Earth,

00:09:09.700 --> 00:09:12.530
our only choice is to build our firepower in multiple areas.

00:09:13.130 --> 00:09:14.400
Not just here?

00:09:14.430 --> 00:09:18.360
That's correct. Our opponents are a regular army.

00:09:18.530 --> 00:09:23.900
Our aim is to stir the Earth Federation Forces to action.

00:09:31.130 --> 00:09:34.630
Oh, jeez. If you move the seat forward, I can fit in here.

00:09:35.360 --> 00:09:36.530
I'm shutting the canopy.

00:09:36.560 --> 00:09:37.700
Go ahead.

00:09:38.560 --> 00:09:41.630
Okay, now gently open the throttle.

00:09:41.660 --> 00:09:42.560
Right.

00:09:46.030 --> 00:09:48.460
Get a feel for the machine's sensitivity.

00:09:48.960 --> 00:09:50.660
That's it. Take off.

00:09:57.030 --> 00:09:59.330
Okay, now cut the auto-balancer.

00:09:59.360 --> 00:10:00.130
Right.

00:10:00.330 --> 00:10:02.960
Are you picking up the coded signal from the Camion?

00:10:03.000 --> 00:10:04.660
I'm still not receiving it.

00:10:07.600 --> 00:10:10.230
I'm curious. What is this?

00:10:10.360 --> 00:10:11.960
Transformation mode.

00:10:12.160 --> 00:10:16.130
Oh, that. The first one raises the mobile suit's head.

00:10:17.060 --> 00:10:18.100
From this fighter?

00:10:18.130 --> 00:10:18.860
Right.

00:10:19.830 --> 00:10:22.230
Don't! You'll kill our speed.

00:10:23.060 --> 00:10:24.330
Then, I'll speed up!

00:10:25.130 --> 00:10:26.100
Üso!

00:10:59.730 --> 00:11:00.500
Haro!

00:11:04.360 --> 00:11:07.060
Miss Marbet! Gotta cut that off!

00:11:12.030 --> 00:11:13.160
Count?

00:11:13.330 --> 00:11:15.600
I just picked up the core fighter's hailing signal.

00:11:16.330 --> 00:11:19.400
Yes, I killed the signal to keep it from being intercepted.

00:11:21.030 --> 00:11:24.400
Okay, when I see the plane, I should turn on the lights, right?

00:11:24.430 --> 00:11:25.260
Haro!

00:11:40.260 --> 00:11:41.960
The core fighter.

00:11:42.460 --> 00:11:43.260
Haro!

00:11:52.800 --> 00:11:54.630
A light! Miss Marbet!

00:11:55.700 --> 00:11:57.400
Those lights weren't on before!

00:11:58.400 --> 00:11:59.330
That's...

00:12:08.500 --> 00:12:11.760
No doubt about it. Those lights are calling us!

00:12:14.100 --> 00:12:17.030
Kill the lights as soon as the wheels are on the ground.

00:12:17.060 --> 00:12:18.060
Yes, sir.

00:12:23.100 --> 00:12:25.160
Miss Marbet's getting better, don't you think?

00:12:25.200 --> 00:12:26.660
Oh, it's not her!

00:12:27.800 --> 00:12:29.800
You're the one who landed it, Üso?!

00:12:29.830 --> 00:12:30.830
Yeah.

00:12:30.900 --> 00:12:33.330
Marbet, is your leg out of action?

00:12:33.700 --> 00:12:35.760
It's just a little numb.

00:12:36.130 --> 00:12:39.460
Leonid! Get another crane over here!

00:12:39.500 --> 00:12:40.630
Well, I'll leave this to you.

00:12:40.660 --> 00:12:42.400
Right. Good job.

00:12:45.530 --> 00:12:47.200
Oh, good! Shahkti!

00:12:52.060 --> 00:12:53.200
What's wrong?

00:12:54.430 --> 00:12:55.560
Üso!

00:12:56.260 --> 00:12:59.660
Silly... I said I'd be okay, didn't I?

00:13:02.100 --> 00:13:04.760
What kind of a child are you?

00:13:05.360 --> 00:13:07.730
What kind? A normal kind.

00:13:08.300 --> 00:13:13.730
This! This is why I have to wear a mask while I'm on Earth.

00:13:13.760 --> 00:13:14.800
Really?

00:13:16.460 --> 00:13:18.030
Looks like you've finished repairs.

00:13:18.060 --> 00:13:22.300
But you won't be able to use the gatling gun unless you land.

00:13:22.400 --> 00:13:23.600
That's what I'd expect.

00:13:24.300 --> 00:13:26.830
But I can use bombs and melee weapons, right?

00:13:26.900 --> 00:13:27.760
Stop.

00:13:27.800 --> 00:13:28.630
Yes, sir.

00:13:29.200 --> 00:13:30.430
What are you doing, sir?

00:13:31.200 --> 00:13:32.760
Launch the Boots first.

00:13:33.730 --> 00:13:34.630
Go ahead!

00:13:35.100 --> 00:13:37.130
A Minovsky control test, right?

00:13:42.400 --> 00:13:44.360
Just going for a morning stroll!

00:13:44.730 --> 00:13:47.660
Ltjg. Cronicle Asher, you can't!

00:13:51.530 --> 00:13:53.530
What? It's taking off?!

00:14:04.030 --> 00:14:04.930
What is it?

00:14:05.200 --> 00:14:09.360
Ltjg. Cronicle Asher just took off in the test unit.

00:14:09.500 --> 00:14:11.060
This early?

00:14:11.160 --> 00:14:12.360
I'm sorry, sir.

00:14:13.460 --> 00:14:15.460
Keep it out of the regular morning report.

00:14:15.500 --> 00:14:18.130
Don't inform Commander Fuala Griffon.

00:14:18.160 --> 00:14:18.930
Sir!

00:14:20.860 --> 00:14:23.860
What's with the old-timey diapers on a line?

00:14:23.900 --> 00:14:27.230
Sorry! That elevator still works?

00:14:27.260 --> 00:14:29.360
Chavarri, you made it!

00:14:29.700 --> 00:14:30.800
You're late!

00:14:30.830 --> 00:14:31.860
Sorry.

00:14:31.900 --> 00:14:33.630
It's been rough here, too, I see.

00:14:33.660 --> 00:14:35.960
We brought a fighter and Top Limb.

00:14:36.000 --> 00:14:39.200
I brought help, so transporting them shouldn't be a problem.

00:14:39.230 --> 00:14:40.560
You're a lifesaver!

00:14:40.800 --> 00:14:41.930
Help, huh?

00:14:41.960 --> 00:14:43.960
Just move it over there!

00:14:48.960 --> 00:14:53.930
I once heard about pilots they used to call Newtypes...

00:14:55.230 --> 00:14:56.300
He couldn't be.

00:15:01.160 --> 00:15:02.860
It's a Zolo-type, one set!

00:15:02.900 --> 00:15:05.460
Helicopter and Boots, coming in from Uwig!

00:15:05.700 --> 00:15:07.000
Sound the alarm!

00:15:07.030 --> 00:15:09.960
It doesn't look like they've noticed us. Maybe they'll leave.

00:15:10.360 --> 00:15:14.630
Roger, but if our support vehicles are headed here, they'll be spotted!

00:15:17.760 --> 00:15:19.130
There's another one.

00:15:20.900 --> 00:15:22.360
And one here, too.

00:15:23.300 --> 00:15:24.630
No, two of them?

00:15:26.900 --> 00:15:30.000
The morning sun makes their shadows easy to spot.

00:15:32.760 --> 00:15:35.000
They're not the refugees from Uwig.

00:15:36.830 --> 00:15:38.960
Trouble! He's starting to turn back!

00:15:39.060 --> 00:15:40.430
Oh, man...

00:15:42.560 --> 00:15:44.530
As I thought, a large truck!

00:15:49.230 --> 00:15:50.960
Is their factory in that direction?

00:15:53.260 --> 00:15:55.260
Come on, let one hit!

00:15:55.760 --> 00:15:56.730
Incoming!

00:15:56.760 --> 00:15:57.930
Lower us!

00:16:05.200 --> 00:16:06.830
Miss Marbet, don't!

00:16:07.630 --> 00:16:10.430
But, it looks like the enemy's bombing us.

00:16:10.460 --> 00:16:12.060
It's okay, I'll go out!

00:16:14.260 --> 00:16:15.630
That kid!

00:16:18.800 --> 00:16:20.030
You like that?

00:16:23.900 --> 00:16:26.960
Where'd that little fighter come from?!

00:16:30.830 --> 00:16:32.500
You're not getting away!

00:16:34.300 --> 00:16:35.300
It's fast!

00:16:36.730 --> 00:16:40.860
You think you have the right to bomb anything and anywhere you like?!

00:16:46.460 --> 00:16:49.130
I'm out of ammo?! Maybe so...

00:16:50.060 --> 00:16:51.230
Something that small...

00:16:58.500 --> 00:17:01.260
He's using air-to-ground missiles in a dogfight?

00:17:01.300 --> 00:17:03.300
You stubborn little... What?!

00:17:05.830 --> 00:17:06.830
The Boots!

00:17:09.330 --> 00:17:10.930
Ground-based fire?

00:17:18.030 --> 00:17:19.760
You really slept, huh?

00:17:20.060 --> 00:17:21.700
Why don't we have some milk now?

00:17:22.960 --> 00:17:24.300
Are you okay?!

00:17:24.330 --> 00:17:25.060
Where's Üso?

00:17:25.100 --> 00:17:26.060
Right!

00:17:26.760 --> 00:17:31.100
Count, we have power! Can you raise the catapult?

00:17:35.200 --> 00:17:37.260
That's the catapult being raised, right?

00:17:38.330 --> 00:17:39.560
Not yet!

00:17:39.730 --> 00:17:40.400
Here he comes!

00:17:40.430 --> 00:17:41.160
Fire!

00:17:41.200 --> 00:17:41.960
Right!

00:17:45.100 --> 00:17:46.460
It's too soon!

00:17:46.960 --> 00:17:48.800
Don't give me that!

00:17:53.600 --> 00:17:55.060
The thing that was on the Camion?!

00:17:55.100 --> 00:17:56.530
Can you hear me, Üso?

00:17:57.730 --> 00:17:59.000
I can.

00:17:59.030 --> 00:18:03.360
Form your fighter up with the Hanger and Boots!

00:18:03.400 --> 00:18:06.000
The Hanger just flew by! Where are the Boots?!

00:18:06.030 --> 00:18:06.860
Here they come!

00:18:06.930 --> 00:18:07.660
Right!

00:18:08.660 --> 00:18:10.560
Set the auto-balancer to V Mode!

00:18:10.600 --> 00:18:11.500
Roger!

00:18:14.830 --> 00:18:16.060
It's docked?

00:18:16.360 --> 00:18:17.900
The Boots are next!

00:18:18.000 --> 00:18:18.730
Right!

00:18:24.630 --> 00:18:26.860
He's docking, too?!

00:18:31.260 --> 00:18:32.230
They shot it?!

00:18:32.860 --> 00:18:33.930
Miss Marbet!

00:18:34.000 --> 00:18:36.800
You heard me! Send out another set of Boots!

00:18:36.830 --> 00:18:38.060
You can do that, right?

00:18:38.330 --> 00:18:41.930
I can't tell where I am if I have to shoot and drive!

00:18:48.930 --> 00:18:51.860
I may have more firepower, but I can barely move now!

00:18:51.900 --> 00:18:53.300
Üso, listen!

00:18:53.330 --> 00:18:54.800
We're sending out another set of Boots!

00:18:55.160 --> 00:18:57.130
They'll launch south of the signal flare.

00:18:57.160 --> 00:18:58.730
Üso, come here!

00:19:02.900 --> 00:19:04.960
Come on, Üso.

00:19:05.930 --> 00:19:08.730
The Minovsky particles shouldn't be that dense here...

00:19:09.830 --> 00:19:10.660
Here he comes.

00:19:11.200 --> 00:19:14.130
Count, prepare to launch! Miss Katejina!

00:19:14.160 --> 00:19:14.960
Right!

00:19:15.900 --> 00:19:17.430
Boots, launch!

00:19:21.600 --> 00:19:23.530
The Boots are right behind you, Üso!

00:19:23.730 --> 00:19:26.260
Roger! Lining up for V Mode!

00:19:35.900 --> 00:19:37.930
Right! Where is he?

00:19:44.160 --> 00:19:45.260
Miss Marbet!

00:19:45.300 --> 00:19:47.830
It should be better than a Shokew, but...

00:19:47.860 --> 00:19:49.500
Did you see that?

00:19:49.960 --> 00:19:51.960
It became a mobile suit!

00:19:55.060 --> 00:19:57.830
It looks like a white mobile suit...

00:19:58.400 --> 00:20:00.030
The white monster?!

00:20:28.060 --> 00:20:31.530
A beam saber?! He wants to go hand-to-hand!

00:20:31.560 --> 00:20:34.260
Well... Well, I can handle that!

00:20:37.130 --> 00:20:38.230
Back at you!

00:20:41.160 --> 00:20:43.960
You! You cat or fox-eyed thing!

00:20:47.660 --> 00:20:50.600
That white monster destroyed my sensors!

00:21:05.430 --> 00:21:08.560
How... How am I still alive?

00:21:23.660 --> 00:21:25.460
Nice landing, Üso.

00:21:26.160 --> 00:21:27.160
Üso...

00:21:27.330 --> 00:21:31.160
Looks like the Victory-type will be useful, Count Nyung.

00:21:31.630 --> 00:21:34.130
Yes. Let's hurry up with the final checks.

00:21:34.760 --> 00:21:36.860
Assemble the mechanics out here!

00:21:36.900 --> 00:21:37.900
Yes, sir!

00:21:38.330 --> 00:21:40.460
Call a crane out here, Odelo!

00:21:40.500 --> 00:21:41.930
Sure thing! Warren!

00:21:42.200 --> 00:21:44.330
The enemy's sure to return, after all.

00:21:57.200 --> 00:22:00.960
Üso, do you understand what you're doing?

00:22:06.830 --> 00:22:09.800
It's only been two or three days,

00:22:09.830 --> 00:22:13.830
and we're already so far from our hometown of Kasarelia...

00:22:24.060 --> 00:22:29.530
Piercing the sky, Blue lightning
sora wo tsukisasu aoi inazuma

00:22:29.530 --> 00:22:35.320
Staining the earth, With the shadow of greed
daichi o someteku, yokubou no kage

00:22:36.370 --> 00:22:41.460
Once again, when the nightmare, Envelops the Earth
futatabi akumu ga, sekai wo tsutsumu toki

00:22:41.460 --> 00:22:46.790
You hear voices crying out "S.O.S."
"SOS" wo sakebu koe ga kikoeru...

00:22:48.630 --> 00:22:54.130
Let proud hope fill your heart
hokoritakaki kibou wo mune ni

00:22:54.720 --> 00:23:03.100
And stand up! Say a prayer for peace!!
tachiagare! heiwa no inori komete!

00:23:04.100 --> 00:23:05.100
WINNERS FOREVER!

00:23:06.100 --> 00:23:08.980
In every age
itsuno jidai mo

00:23:08.980 --> 00:23:14.570
...People take risks for freedom
hito wa jiyuu wo kakete

00:23:15.000 --> 00:23:17.000
WINNERS FOREVER!

00:23:18.330 --> 00:23:21.240
The battle goes on
tatakai tsuzukeru

00:23:21.240 --> 00:23:25.920
Fighting all alone in solitude
kodoku na made ni hitori...

00:23:34.830 --> 00:23:38.930
If Üso hadn't grabbed onto that orange mobile suit that day...

00:23:39.260 --> 00:23:41.400
If he hadn't met that pilot...

00:23:42.300 --> 00:23:44.700
Then what happened today could have been avoided.

00:23:45.930 --> 00:23:49.660
But, Üso did all he could to overcome the danger.

00:23:51.160 --> 00:23:53.800
Next time, on Mobile Suit Victory Gundam:

00:23:54.260 --> 00:23:54.410
"The Day He Met The Machine".

00:23:54.410 --> 00:23:56.160
Next Episode THE DAY HE MET THE MACHINE

00:23:56.160 --> 00:23:57.700
Please watch it!
